_Anyone_ can create Excalibur via #dipping; however, only Lawful
characters may become the Hand of Elbereth.  Go ahead, knock yourself
out.  Perfectly all right to use any artifact, no matter what your
alignment (idea for the dev team, perhaps.. make penalties for using
non-aligned weapons.)
As far as the crysknife/enchanting decision, _personally_ I'd go for
enchanting Excalibur.  Artifacts are better than crysknives... well at
least Excalibur definitely is.
There are two ways to get Stormbringer that I know of... Wish for it
(natrually) and #offer sacrifices to your good old Morrigan.  There's no
telling how long or how many sacrifices it will take.  Some games, I
have sacrificed until my brain melted, and my luck soared, but no
Stormy...  Other times, I've started a game, killed a newt, dragged the
corpse over to the handy-dandy altar of <insert your favorite chaotic
god here> that just happened to be on the first level, and CLANG..
Stormbringer!
Of course.. a first level character with Stormbringer still gets munched
pretty easy...

